From 622143eb1a4a43cc6fc60af7d42ff3991631756d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:43:16 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui): Stop never takes over a typed turn; ordinary Stop
 always runs; anchored :auto=

Round-3 review of #3908:
- _end_background_turn: on a turn-end-request-v1 gateway an unstamped holder is a typed
  turn: nothing is ended or taken over, and the chat is told so. session.take_over is
  only for an older (not capable) gateway with nothing queued.
- session.interrupt always runs the ordinary idle Stop (automation replays, post-turn
  review) and starts the background worker in addition; background_turn is a hint.
- holder_auto_kind reads only the segment right before the last :platform=, so a
  client-chosen session/task id cannot fake the stamp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
